    "title": "Halo",
    "source": {
        "kind": "custom",
        "note": "A HUD over a live background: a deep night-navy ground, windows of dark smoked glass that let the wave behind them glow through, pale ink for text and one sky blue as the signal. Board hues — violet, amber, emerald and rose — sit beside the sky in charts and tags at the same lightness so no board shouts. Taken from the halo HUD itself (2026-09-25). Light is a designed daylight counterpart with the same sky signal, not an inverted night."
